+## M-01: Meter framework substitutions
+
+Source: pinned [Meter parts](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/tree/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/meter) and [useRegisteredLabelId](https://github.com/mui/base-ui/blob/47b40521eab921c2756bf9bdb0b0f07fbfdb8c8c/packages/react/src/utils/useRegisteredLabelId.ts). Native class, string CSS, snippets, bindings/attachments and events follow the accepted framework substitutions in T-01; initially undefined refs follow A-01. Typed context exposes derived values, Svelte-stable IDs preserve relationships, and post-mount label registration retains SSR omission followed by hydration association. Public named part Props/State retain required numeric value and empty state. Replacement snippets explicitly preserve Root's hidden presentation x and Value's output.
+
+Rationale: implement the actual pin with a private Meter dependency closure, including NaN/clamping and atypical bound arithmetic. No local behavioral correction or shared helper extraction is included. The [compatibility register](../parity/meter/compatibility.md), [feature docs](meter.md) and [assertion record](../parity/meter/README.md) distinguish 22 ordinary candidates, four separate parameterized variants, full conformance and supplemental evidence. Shared aggregate credits remain unchanged. Decision status: proposed in [PR #32](https://github.com/sveltery/base/pull/32), within the accepted framework baseline; no additional behavioral deviation decision, complete assistive-technology parity or final merge eligibility is claimed. Full integrated-head tests, secured paired browsers, public consumers and independent/configured automatic reviews remain required.
